            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for is that so?; all right then, then the Hindi for that'll do, that works."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Build two answers about yourself: मैं हिंदी बोलता हूँ and मैं भारत में रहता हूँ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ताला",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ताला — tālā — \"a lock\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ताला (tālā) is a tadbhava, a word inherited from Sanskrit and reshaped by sound change. It comes from tāla, \"latch, bolt\" (CDIAL 5749). CDIAL compares a Tamil word for \"bar, bolt, latch\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
